                <pb facs="0081" n="71" xml:id="pg71"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/574: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cramp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-08T12:00:00-06:00">September 8,
                        1937—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 5:13 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>57. For Duggan. Referring to our conversation this morning, I have suggested to
                    Castleman that he obtain some statement from President Somoza with reference to
                    his desire for reciprocal withdrawal of the stamps, which could be quoted direct
                    to the President of Honduras tomorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Cramp</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
